// Promoted 2026-08-15 from graphix-fuzz/fuzz/crashes/crash_000022.gx
// (see 00 for the backlog audit). The BRANCHING shape of the same
// invariant: two self-calls per level, the first with a constant
// argument that never approaches the base case, so the derivation is
// an unbounded binary tree rather than a chain. It must still settle
// on the depth limit's bottom rather than overflow — the recursion
// ruling retains transient instances unconditionally, so a shape that
// both branches AND never terminates is the memory-hungriest way to
// reach the bound.
{let rec fib = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => i64:0, i64:1 => i64:1, _ => fib(i64:2) + fib(n - i64:2)}; fib(i64:12)}
